Article 5 (Wearing of Formal Uniforms)
(1) The formal uniform attire of juvenile reformatory personnel, etc. shall consist of the following: <Amended on December 27, 2007; March 27, 2019>
1. A formal uniform;
2. Work shoes;
3. A name tag;
4. Chest insignia;
5. Deleted. <October 20, 2016>
6. Deleted. <October 20, 2016>
7. Deleted. <October 20, 2016>
(2) Formal uniforms shall be worn in any of the following cases: <Amended on October 20, 2016; March 27, 2019>
1. When performing ordinary duties;
2. When attending events, including celebrations or commemorative ceremonies;
3. When reporting an assumption of or departure from office;
4. In other cases determined by the head of a juvenile reformatory or juvenile classification review center (hereinafter referred to as the "Director").
